      ],
      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.455
      ],
      "seconds": 20.35,
      "text": "Your DNA carries a timestamp. Chemical marks accumulate on it with age, and they can be read like a clock. In October, a team in Bonn took blood cells from an eighty year old donor. They reprogrammed them directly into neural stem cells. Then they read the clock again. It said under twenty.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 8,
        "pitch": 0
      },
      "clips": [
        {
          "src": "videos/11-epigenetic-clock-reset/v2-1.mp3",
